there are tons of habitats that scientists haven't studied in this way. But the point is... These are fully functioning reefs. They contain all the animals that you would expect to see on a myriad of natural reefs, which begs the question, is it in the interests of the people of California to blow up a fully functioning reef and destroy it. In 2010, the California legislature decided it wasn't and they passed AB 2503,

